{"id": "EUVD-2026-108865", "enisaUuid": "abf8cbdb-8151-3c30-bb6d-1b700e6104d7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: cpsw_new: unregister devlink on port registration failure\n\ncpsw_probe() registers devlink before registering the CPSW ports.\n\nIf cpsw_register_ports() fails, the error path only unregisters the\nnotifiers and then releases the lower level resources. It does not undo\nthe successful cpsw_register_devlink() call, leaving the devlink instance\nand its parameters registered after probe has failed.\n\nAdd a devlink cleanup label for the path where devlink registration has\nalready succeeded, and use it when port registration fails.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b020390b4ef39adc40c800301042baf812280da1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a5ac0defdd42e566f1c871272370b6a3a8eef5c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43d4af5c5331ea739a49cb1097d41e502ed91ec4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8af61d5bd87fd1a3bdc81fe948e7acdc8aa5bcf0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2bcf21ede6b097ca96cb1f7679761acca6510555", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a44945b0d3422f5d81b49c97e293f3e21a8c585", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b64f763b607426ac97e44b114f0b8844ac3b86dd", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98909"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7h76-g88g-x9j7", "CVE-2026-98909"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "002bcd8d-116d-34a4-9edc-f63e4006b5f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "0114d523-2c25-30a9-a4b0-5c260e4e0602", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <2bcf21ede6b097ca96cb1f7679761acca6510555"}, {"id": "136ce958-cd85-3e56-ac68-649aac87e825", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch